          "sourceHref": "сontent/i2d796693-f9b7-4487-8cbd-425a984159be/Research Methodology.html",
          "resourceKind": "html",
          "contentBody": "Basic Page\nResearch Methodology\nPsychologists have a range of options when studying developmental psychology.  Three major categories of research methodology they may use include:- descriptive research (includes naturalistic observation, surveys, and case studies)- correlational research- experimental research\nEach of these main categories will be discussed in turn.\n(this link opens in a new window/tab)",
