          "moduleVisibilityLabel": "visible",
          "sourceHref": "сontent/i5725204e-4491-4b5f-8701-d49a6cf6fac3/Steps for Making a Bar Graph.html",
          "resourceKind": "html",
          "contentBody": "Steps for Making a Bar Graph\nOn graph paper, draw a set of axes (x and y).  Be sure to leave room for titles and headings and use as much of the page as you can when you draw the axes.\nGive the graph a title.\nLabel the horizontal axis (x-axis) with the manipulated variable.  Include each category of the manipulated variable under the appropriate bar.\nLabel the vertical axis (y-axis) with the responding variable.  Add a scale that marks the value of the responding variable.\nFor each manipulated variable, draw a solid bar to the height of the corresponding value of the dependent variable.  In the example below, each activity (manipulated variable) requires a box be drawn to the level of blinks (the responding variable).\nData from the table below will be used to create the bar graph.\nBlinks per Minute\nTrial 1\nTrial 2\nTrial 3\nAverage\n8\n9\n7\n8\n7\n8\n6\n7\n12\n10\n11\n11\n22\n18\n20\n20",
