          "resourceKind": "html",
          "contentBody": "Basic Page\nUnderstanding Graphs\nSelect and work through the Understanding Graphs (Entertainment) activity using the following link (you may need to click Understanding Graphs under the Statistics and Probability column first): Understanding Graphs - LearnAlberta  (use login: LA15 pswd: 3950 if prompted)\nWork through each topic.  You may need to select the Topics button at the top to access the lessons:\nAlternatively, if the website will not work properly, access the content using the following PowerPoint presentation (this does not include the interactive portion of the lessons):\nAs you complete the four topics in Understanding Graphs, record in your notebook your responses to the following questions:\n What is the importance of titles for graphic displays?\n What vertical scale makes it easiest to determine the number of roller coasters per country? Why?\nWhat is the benefit of arranging the number of roller coasters by country?\nIn the skiing example, which value implies the greatest cost increase - the graph with $5.00 increments or the graph with $10.00 increments?\nWhat are the advantages and disadvantages of pie charts (circle graphs) and bar graphs?\n What are the main features of histograms and bar charts as described in the exercises?",
